        "step_anchor": "step-1",
        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When we want to multiply two binomials, we take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.</p>",
            "readable_text": "When we want to multiply two binomials, we take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, to multiply <span class=\"math\">[MATH: ({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x + 2),]</span> we multiply <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}{x}}]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x + 2),]</span> and then we add this to the product of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}{3}}]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x+2)]</span>:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, to multiply [MATH: ({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})] and [MATH: (x + 2),] we multiply [MATH: {\\color{blue}{x}}] and [MATH: (x + 2),] and then we add this to the product of [MATH: {\\color{red}{3}}] and [MATH: (x+2)]:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})(x + 2) &amp;= \\[5pt]\n{\\color{blue}{x}}(x + 2) + {\\color{red}{3}}(x + 2) &amp;= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 2x + 3x + 6 &amp;= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 5x + 6\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\n{\\color{blue}{x}}(x + 2) + {\\color{red}{3}}(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 2x + 3x + 6 &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 5x + 6\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWhen we want to multiply two binomials, we take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\nContent:\nFor example, to multiply [MATH: ({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})] and [MATH: (x + 2),] we multiply [MATH: {\\color{blue}{x}}] and [MATH: (x + 2),] and then we add this to the product of [MATH: {\\color{red}{3}}] and [MATH: (x+2)]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\n{\\color{blue}{x}}(x + 2) + {\\color{red}{3}}(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 2x + 3x + 6 &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 5x + 6\n}]"
      },
