    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWhen we want to multiply two binomials, we take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\nContent:\nFor example, to multiply [MATH: ({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})] and [MATH: (x + 2),] we multiply [MATH: {\\color{blue}{x}}] and [MATH: (x + 2),] and then we add this to the product of [MATH: {\\color{red}{3}}] and [MATH: (x+2)]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\n{\\color{blue}{x}}(x + 2) + {\\color{red}{3}}(x + 2) &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 2x + 3x + 6 &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 + 5x + 6\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Binomials\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand and simplify [MATH: (y + 5)(y - 2).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(y + 5)(y - 2) &= \\\ny(y-2) + 5(y-2) &=\\\ny^2-2y +5y-10 &=\\\ny^2 + 3y - 10\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (q + 6)(q + 2) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 9q^{2} + 12]\nb. [MATH: q^{2} + 12]\nc. [MATH: q + 8]\nd. [MATH: 9q + 12]\ne. [MATH: q^{2} + 8q + 12]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nExpand the following product of binomials. Write your answer in standard form.[MATH: (b + 7)(b \u2212 2) =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Binomials with Leading Coefficients\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand and simplify [MATH: (2n - 1)(3n - 6).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(2n - 1)(3n - 6) &= \\\n2n(3n - 6) + (-1)(3n - 6) &= \\\n6n^2 - 12n - 3n + 6 &= \\\n6n^2 - 15n + 6\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nExpand the following product of binomials. Write your answer in standard form.[MATH: (2x + 5)(3x + 1) =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3x + 2)(5x \u2212 4) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 15x^{2} \u2212 8]\nb. [MATH: 15x^{2} + 22x \u2212 8]\nc. [MATH: 15x^{2} \u2212 2x \u2212 8]\nd. [MATH: 15x^{2} + 2x \u2212 8]\ne. [MATH: 15x^{2} + 2x + 8]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Binomials with Higher Powers and Multiple Variables\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (p^2-q^2)(2p+3q).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n[MATH: (p^{2} \u2212 q^{2})(2p + 3q)|=; p^{2}(2p + 3q) + (\u2212 q^{2})(2p + 3q)|=; 2p^{3} + 3p^{2}q \u2212 2pq^{2} \u2212 3q^{3}]\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms.\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (5a + b)(a + 3b) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5a^{2} + 16ab + 3b^{2}]\nb. [MATH: a^{2} + 16ab + b^{2}]\nc. [MATH: 5a^{2} + 12ab + b^{2}]\nd. [MATH: 5a^{2} + 14ab + 3b^{2}]\ne. [MATH: a^{2} + 14ab + 3b^{2}]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (7u^{2} \u2212 6v)(v \u2212 u) =][FREE_ENTRY 1][MATH: u^{3} +]\n[FREE_ENTRY 2][MATH: u^{2}v +]\n[FREE_ENTRY 3][MATH: uv \u2212]\n[FREE_ENTRY 4][MATH: v^{2}]"
